From: Developer <dev@example.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Sep 2024 10:05:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] drm/amd/display: Improve HDMI audio adapter compatibility for BC-250

Some HDMI audio extractors and older receivers fail to parse the audio
info frame correctly when driven by the Cyan Skillfish display engine.
This patch forces a standard info frame packet formatting for this
specific ASIC.

Signed-off-by: Developer <dev@example.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/core/dc_resource.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/core/dc_resource.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/core/dc_resource.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/core/dc_resource.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/core/dc_resource.c
@@ -200,6 +200,11 @@ void resource_build_info_frame(struct pipe_ctx *pipe_ctx)
 {
 	// ...
+	if (pipe_ctx->stream->ctx->asic_id.chip_family == FAMILY_YELLOW_CARP) {
+		/* Force basic audio info frame for BC-250 */
+		info_frame->audio_info_frame.channel_count = 2;
+	}
 	// ...
 }

